cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the version you used."
title: "GeoMapper (geoMap v2): cartographic visualisation in base MATLAB for GRACE-like gravimetry"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Weigelt
    given-names: Matthias
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/matweigelt/GeoMapper"
license: MIT
version: "2.0.516"
date-released: "2026-08-22"
keywords:
  - MATLAB
  - cartography
  - map projections
  - GRACE
  - satellite gravimetry
  - equivalent water height
  - mascon
abstract: >-
  Publication-quality cartographic visualisation in base MATLAB, with no
  toolbox dependencies, aimed at GRACE-like satellite gravimetry products:
  equivalent water height fields, mascon solutions, trend maps with
  significance masking, and along-track and time-series displays. Sixteen
  map projections are implemented forward and inverse on a spherical
  Earth, each validated against published worked examples, an independent
  projection library, and analytic invariants.
notes: >-
  ORCID above is a placeholder and must be completed before any release
  that is cited. The patch component of the version tracks the count of
  verified test points, so it moves when the evidence moves and a pure
  rename bumps nothing.
